  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Maryland received $180M in federal contract obligations in FY2027 to date. Obligations fell 99.5% year over year. Award activity to date shows 723 awards with an average award size of $249K. Fiscal-year comparisons show prior full-year totals of $42.1B in FY22, $41.7B in FY23, $46.3B in FY24, $39.7B in FY25, and $37.2B in FY26. Research and Development in the Physical, Engineering, and Life Sciences (except Nanotechnology and Biotechnology) is the largest industry by obligations, receiving $89.4M. The National Aeronautics and Space Administration is the largest buying agency so far, obligating $89.5M. THE JOHNS HOPKINS UNIVERSITY APPLIED PHYSICS LABORATORY LLC is the largest vendor so far, receiving $85.3M. Construction, information technology services, and telecommunications also appear among the top industries by obligations. These figures are partial because FY2027 totals are fiscal year to date.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "What changed versus prior fiscal years?",
        "body": "Obligations fell 99.5% year over year. FY27 to date obligations are $180M compared with prior full-year totals: FY22 $42.1B, FY23 $41.7B, FY24 $46.3B, FY25 $39.7B, and FY26 $37.2B. The number of awards to date is 723 and the average award size is $249K. These FY2027 totals are fiscal year to date and therefore partial."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Who are the top agencies and vendors right now?",
        "body": "The National Aeronautics and Space Administration obligated $89.5M and the Department of Veterans Affairs obligated $48.5M. THE JOHNS HOPKINS UNIVERSITY APPLIED PHYSICS LABORATORY LLC received $85.3M and MATOS-GRUNLEY JOINT VENTURE received $21.4M. Other notable buyers include the General Services Administration with $20.3M and the Department of Health and Human Services with $11.9M. Top industries include Research and Development with $89.4M and Commercial and Institutional Building Construction with $28.8M."
      }
    ]
  },
